  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "When Fang Yuan arrives, Wan Liang Han greets him as Suan Bu Jin with a leisurely expression and says he has waited quite a while. Narration names him the wisdom path Gu Immortal who lured Fang Yuan, and notes he had been repeatedly deducing Fang Yuan despite emperor yama’s protection. Together with Wan Xiao he activates killer moves to protect Wan Hao Guang when soul beasts besiege them.",
      "chapters": [
        1799
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "char_wan_xiao",
        "char_wan_hao_guang"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "His forehead is swollen and he has an ugly appearance, though he smiles while speaking.",
      "chapters": [
        1799
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "When Fang Yuan turns from defense to attack, Wan Liang Han feels a chill and regrets that Wan clan provoked such a person. He warns Wan Xiao to retreat and joins him in activating wisdom obstacle Immortal Gu. Fang Yuan’s true target is Wan Liang Han. Immortal killer move Wisdom Grasp sends a great thief ghost hand into his body, and he dies with eyes wide open. Later Wan clan talk places him as rank seven and a Western Desert righteous path Gu Immortal whose death is a heavy loss.",
      "chapters": [
        1801
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
